## 5. TRAVEL FATIGUE SYSTEM

Frequent travel is one of the most underestimated performance risks for founders. A 3-day domestic trip with 2 late nights and 2 hotel sleeps can leave a founder running at 60–70% capacity for 4–5 days after they return — without ever knowing it.

### Detection Markers:

| Signal | Threshold | Why |
|---|---|---|
| HRV drop | >15% below 7-day baseline | Circadian disruption suppresses parasympathetic activity |
| RHR elevation | +5–8 bpm above baseline for 2+ days | Body is clearing travel stress load |
| Sleep efficiency | <75% on travel nights | Unfamiliar environment, noise, light disruption |
| Recovery crash | Green→Yellow or Yellow→Red within 48 hrs | Compound effect of travel stressors |
| Skin temp deviation | +0.5°C or more | Inflammatory response to travel, food, environment |
| SpO2 | Below 95% on travel nights | Cabin pressure, air quality, disrupted breathing |

### Travel Fatigue Score Formula:

```
Score = (HRV % below baseline × 0.4)
      + (RHR % above baseline × 0.3)
      + (sleep efficiency delta × 0.2)
      + (recovery score delta × 0.1)

0–30:   Mild     → 1-day recovery protocol
31–60:  Moderate → 2–3 day protocol
61+:    High     → Full recovery before any output push
```

### Recovery Protocol (in this exact order):

1. **Sleep first** — Earlier bedtime, no screens 60min before, dark and cool room (<23°C)
2. **Morning light** — Sunlight within 30 minutes of waking. Resets the suprachiasmatic nucleus. The single fastest circadian anchor.
3. **Hydration** — 500ml water immediately on waking. No alcohol for 48 hours post-travel.
4. **Strain cap** — Keep below 10 regardless of recovery score for 24 hours
5. **Decision deferral** — If travel fatigue score >40, defer all high-stakes irreversible decisions by 48 hours

