## 10. THE NUMBERS THAT CHANGED HOW I WORK

After 30+ days of daily Bheem briefs, these are the patterns that became undeniable:

**1. HRV predicts my best days 12–18 hours in advance.**
When I wake up to a brief showing HRV >47ms and recovery >70%, I know before I start work that I have a high-performance day. I schedule my hardest conversations and deepest work on those days. The output quality difference is visible.

**2. Travel costs me 3–4 days, not 1.**
I used to think I "recovered" from a 2-day trip in a day. The data showed my HRV didn't return to baseline until day 4 post-travel in many cases. I now block no major strategic decisions for 48 hours after any travel longer than one night away.

**3. Sleep consistency matters more than duration.**
My 72% consistency score (Apr 30 data) was doing more damage than my 6h 44min duration. The body's circadian rhythm is not a metaphor — it is a literal timing system. Disrupting it degrades all sleep quality even when you get enough hours.

**4. The recovery drop always preceded the stress event, not followed it.**
In 3 out of 4 fundraising-related recovery crashes, my HRV started declining 2–3 days *before* the most stressful call or meeting. The body was sensing load the mind hadn't consciously registered yet.

**5. The CEO Action is the metric that matters most.**
Every other health app tells me I'm green or yellow. None of them told me "don't sign that term sheet today." Bheem does. That's the entire point.

